                    </span>
                    <ul>
                      <li>
                        In the scope of LLMs prompting, we define KEYTOKENS as the tokens with the most positive contributions to the answer: 
                      </li>
                      <li v-html="renderFormula('$K(x,y)=\\begin{cases}\\{ x_i \\mid C(x_i,y) > 0 \\}, \\text{if less than }\\beta \\\\ \\{ x_i \\mid N(C(x_i,y)) > \\alpha \\}, \\text{otherwise}\\end{cases}$')">
                      </li>
                      <li>
                        Specifically, we first normalize (i.e., N (·, ·)) the positive contribution values, 
                        and then select tokens whose normalized positive contributions exceed a threshold α. 
                        In practice, positive contribution tokens can be very few. 
                        To address this situation, when there are fewer than a predefined proportion of the total tokens β, 
                        we directly take them as KEYTOKENS.
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                </el-row>
